\chapter{The \texttt{cli.signupsheets} module and
         the \texttt{signupsheets} subcommands}%
\label{cli.signupsheets}

In this chapter we introduce the subcommands found under [[nytid signupsheets]],
it's the [[cli.signupsheets]] module.

The CLI loads every subcommand module at start-up, so whatever this
module imports at the top level is paid for by every nytid invocation,
not just the signupsheets commands.
The heavy dependencies---[[nytid.schedules]] with its calendar stack
and the [[nytid.signup]] modules---are therefore imported inside the
functions that use them, module-style ([[from nytid.signup import
sheets]]), so that tests patching attributes on the source modules
still take effect at call time.
Only the cheap course-lookup modules stay at the top, because
[[hr]] and [[schedule]] import [[SIGNUPSHEET_URL_PATH]] and
[[complete_signup_users]] from here at module scope and those must
not trigger the heavy imports.
<<[[signupsheets.py]]>>=
